  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Point of intersection of the two given curves are <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>0,0</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> and <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>a</mi></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/3456789865e45678gchjb.JPG\" style=\"max-width:100%; object-fit:contain\" style=\"width: 190px; height: 167px;\" /><br />The area bounded&nbsp;<math><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mrow><msubsup><mo stretchy=\"false\">∫</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi>a</mi></mrow></msubsup><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi>a</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><msubsup><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mfrac><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mrow><mn>12</mn><mi>a</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mn>0</mn><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi>a</mi></mrow></msubsup></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>8</mn><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>16</mn><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mn>3</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>16</mn><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mn>3</mn></mfrac></math>&nbsp;sq. units<br />Given,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>16</mn><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>64</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></math></p><p>Hence, the positive value of&nbsp;<math><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math></p>",
